---
import EditorialLayout from '../layouts/EditorialLayout.astro';
import ActionIcon from '../components/editorial/ActionIcon.astro';
import Evidence from '../components/editorial/Evidence.astro';
import CareerTimeline from '../components/editorial/CareerTimeline.astro';
import CampaignFigure from '../components/editorial/CampaignFigure.astro';
import { profile, testimonials } from '../content/editorial.js';
import { certifications } from '../content/site.js';
const recommendations = [testimonials[1], testimonials[2], testimonials[0]];
---
<EditorialLayout home>
  <section class="opening wrap" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div>
      <p class="dateline">Pan Asia Bank · Colombo · 2023</p>
      <h1 id="intro-title">Which enquiries <em>became loans?</em></h1>
      <p class="opening-lede">I had US$25,000 to spend on gold loan ads. Before I split it between Google and Meta, I wanted to hear from the people answering the enquiries.</p>
      <p>The bank’s sales team said the Meta leads were better. I put 60% of the budget there. Six months of ads later, the bank counted 259 funded loans.</p>
      <div class="byline"><img src="/images/andrew-fonseka-240.webp" width="48" height="48" alt="" /><div><strong>Andrew Fonseka, MBA</strong><span>Paid media specialist · Greater Vancouver</span></div></div>
      <div class="story-links"><a href="/case-studies/panasia/">Inside the Gold2Cash campaign <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a><a href={profile.resume}>View résumé (PDF)</a></div>
    </div>
    <CampaignFigure campaign="panasia" priority />
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="agency wrap chapter">
    <p class="dateline">Kites Global · Retail &amp; e-commerce</p>
    <h2>Same agency. <em>Different briefs.</em></h2>
    <p class="chapter-intro">Pan Asia Bank was one of four accounts I managed at Kites Global. For Petmart, the question was how much a first order brought in. For Godrej, it was how to introduce a hair colour to shoppers in India.</p>
    <div class="print-spread">
      <article><CampaignFigure campaign="petmart" /><h3>What was a first order worth?</h3><p>I built Petmart’s Merchant Center feed and split Shopping and Performance Max by new and returning buyers. On US$5,000 in spend, the client reported four dollars in first-order sales for every dollar spent.</p><a class="read" href="/case-studies/petmart/">Read the Petmart figures <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></article>
      <article><CampaignFigure campaign="godrej" /><h3>A launch with 30 creators.</h3><p>I helped shape the Godrej Expert Rich Crème launch and ran the Meta and YouTube ads behind the creator programme. Godrej attributed about US$350,000 in sales to paid media that quarter.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="marginal"><strong>At the smaller end of my client list</strong> I built a Shopify store and product feed for a Sri Lankan apparel retailer. At about US$850 a month, Shopping and Meta beat its target of 100+ retailer leads by 20%.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities" class="chapter inhouse"><div class="wrap two-column">
    <div><p class="dateline">Aegon · Canada &amp; U.S. · 2025–26</p><h2>Ten to twenty campaigns <em>in a day.</em></h2>
    <p>Moving in-house meant co-managing a seven-figure annual budget. Each launch needed a name the reporting team could use, tracking that worked, and a compliance review.</p>
    <p>I wrote a Google Apps Script builder with AI coding tools. A marketer could enter a brief once and get campaign names, tracking links, ad copy drafts and A/B variants ready for review.</p>
    <a class="read" href="/case-studies/aegon/">Follow a campaign through the builder <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></div>
    <div class="ledger" aria-label="Campaign builder usage"><div><strong>22</strong><span>colleagues used the builder</span></div><div><strong>~200</strong><span>campaigns launched through it</span></div><div><strong>12 days</strong><span>of work saved per year, estimated</span></div></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wrap chapter">
    <p class="dateline">Freelance · Education · 2026</p>
    <h2>Two colleges still <em>had seats to fill.</em></h2>
    <div class="two-column">
      <div><p class="chapter-intro">While I was at Aegon, I took on education projects with my employer’s approval. A Saudi university had an intake problem you could easily miss in Ads Manager.</p>
        <p>Its broad Meta campaign brought in 603 leads. Only 17 students from that campaign paid their fees at the two colleges with the most seats left. Working through a partner agency, I advised on, helped build and managed the campaigns, including a dedicated higher-intent form for those colleges.</p>
        <p>The dedicated campaign brought in 161 leads. This time, 125 paid their fees at the priority colleges. The university matched the enrolments in its admissions CRM.</p>
        <a class="read" href="/case-studies/university/">See how admissions counted enrolments <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div><Evidence />
    </div>
    <div class="marginal"><h3>At DIMO Academy, the budget stayed at US$900 a month.</h3><p>I built a landing page and a shorter enquiry form, set up Microsoft Advertising and helped install a chat assistant. The academy counted 212 qualified leads from March to May, up from 178 the quarter before.</p><a class="read" href="/case-studies/dats/">Read about the DIMO rebuild <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a></div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="wrap chapter two-column">
    <div><p class="dateline">About Andrew</p><h2>From Colombo <em>to Vancouver.</em></h2>
      <p>I started at Enfection, supporting campaigns in Sri Lanka, Singapore and Malaysia. By 2023 I was managing four client accounts at Kites Global and supporting five more. I earned my MBA at University Canada West in 2024, then joined Aegon in Langley.</p>
      <p>I’m available now for hybrid or remote paid media specialist and coordinator roles in Greater Vancouver. I speak English and Sinhala and am authorized to work in Canada.</p>
      <details id="toolkit" class="credentials"><summary>Tools and certifications</summary><p>I work in Google Ads, Meta, LinkedIn, Microsoft Advertising and TikTok Ads. For measurement I use GA4, Google Tag Manager, Enhanced Conversions, Meta Conversions API and CRM data from tools including HubSpot.</p><ul>{certifications.map(c=><li>{c.title} · {c.issuer}{c.year && ' (' + c.year + ')'}</li>)}</ul></details>
      <div class="story-links"><a href={profile.resume}>Read my résumé (PDF)</a><a href={profile.portfolio}>View the portfolio (PDF)</a></div>
    </div><CareerTimeline />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap recommendations chapter" aria-labelledby="recommendations-title">
    <h2 id="recommendations-title">In their words.</h2>
    <div class="recommendation-grid">{recommendations.map(t=><figure class="recommendation-card">
      <blockquote><p>“{t.excerpt}”</p></blockquote><figcaption><div><strong>{t.name}</strong><span>{t.role}</span></div></figcaption>
      <details><summary>Full recommendation</summary><p>“{t.quote}”</p></details>
    </figure>)}</div>
    <a class="read" href={profile.linkedin + 'details/recommendations/'}>Recommendations on LinkedIn <ActionIcon name="arrow" /></a>
  </section>
</EditorialLayout>
